                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8c83e5c0-1b42-3f8b-b645-eadf69e506f8",
                        "entry_id": "0bb946ca-80e1-3970-9e3c-41c1f74f356b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "палеонт. ископаемый высший примат, считающийся одним из предков человека; род семейства гоминиды"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9324b5ec-9591-4f20-a3e0-04b75b83ea81",
                                "sense_id": "8c83e5c0-1b42-3f8b-b645-eadf69e506f8",
                                "text": "Австралопитек жил в эпоху, когда ситуация с магнитными полюсами была противоположной нынешней."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c058d67c-7072-4866-a7cd-066e629607c9",
                        "source_entry_id": "0bb946ca-80e1-3970-9e3c-41c1f74f356b",
                        "source_sense_id": "8c83e5c0-1b42-3f8b-b645-eadf69e506f8",
                        "target_lang_word": "australopithecus",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "australopithecus",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "29e950ec-6d9f-325a-b84b-bbd625a816b4",
                                        "entry_id": "d47f3f75-d6b6-3af9-93b2-bc75ea7231f8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative letter-case form of Australopithecus."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8fe3f768-3456-452c-aa89-ef259513c180",
                                                "sense_id": "29e950ec-6d9f-325a-b84b-bbd625a816b4",
                                                "text": "The Ramapithecus line divided into two australopitheci which also died out, and the ancestor of modern man, which gradually evolved into Homo sapiens"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fbd64390-3331-4f26-9138-1759ac26956d",
                                                "sense_id": "29e950ec-6d9f-325a-b84b-bbd625a816b4",
                                                "text": "If ramidus or one of the early australopithecuses, A. anamensis or A. afarensis, has a rather apelike vestibular system, as you might expect, then the old argument about mosaic evolution can be raised."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "79c9fda7-3bb7-4b76-b898-e797b862ed19",
                                                "sense_id": "29e950ec-6d9f-325a-b84b-bbd625a816b4",
                                                "text": "He also puts forth unfounded claims like the one that australopitheci had prehensile feet like chimps and not feet like men, enabling them to walk upright."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2f7ddddf-9193-46e8-9284-abfe2b546bc0",
                                                "sense_id": "29e950ec-6d9f-325a-b84b-bbd625a816b4",
                                                "text": "His hyperrealistic sculptural installations have typically looked to gut the preconceived notions about bravery and honor with which monumental sculpture is infused—whether in the vomiting boy scouts cut off from their chaperones in Lost and Sick (1996–2001), or the comically pathetic scenario of Very, Very First Man: Necessary Alterations (1998–99), in which a pair of recently evolved australopitheci clumsily reattach each other’s tails in a vain attempt to return to lower (and presumably less responsibility-burdened) life forms."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "24fe4091-aa0e-4ea0-b5bd-fd257062f560",
                        "source_entry_id": "0bb946ca-80e1-3970-9e3c-41c1f74f356b",
                        "source_sense_id": "8c83e5c0-1b42-3f8b-b645-eadf69e506f8",
                        "target_lang_word": "australopith",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "australopith",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8f38a033-ea0c-3b5e-a999-c81ee931c0f8",
                                        "entry_id": "db216915-a644-327e-b064-21263ddf4740",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of the hominids of the extinct genus Australopithecus."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af9dd0e2-ccfa-4a2f-840b-8ea457b05d36",
                                                "sense_id": "8f38a033-ea0c-3b5e-a999-c81ee931c0f8",
                                                "text": "The incisors are more similar in size to the molars compared to earlier australopiths—a condition which is also more humanlike.\nThe limb bones indicate A. garhi had small stature like earlier australopiths."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95e31638-508c-47d7-b581-e38fe9807f40",
                                                "sense_id": "8f38a033-ea0c-3b5e-a999-c81ee931c0f8",
                                                "text": "Most authorities would nowadays concur that the australopiths were generally committed to habitats with at least some trees, to which they were more or less tied for sleeping and for shelter from predators during the day, as well as for a large part of their sustenance."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8048356-5770-485e-b495-3b841f825b21",
                                                "sense_id": "8f38a033-ea0c-3b5e-a999-c81ee931c0f8",
                                                "text": "Later we'll consider how these principles apply to australopith craniofacial function, but first let's review briefly how different australopiths accommodated large teeth and big masticatory muscles, and how they grew large, buttressed faces."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "australopith",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9004bfcf-c260-358f-a83c-fe54986dcc31",
                                        "entry_id": "57455eba-23aa-33fc-a646-4624e7baae95",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or pertaining to the hominids of the extinct genus Australopithecus."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f3068128-90bb-49ec-aeac-ed99fcb897d0",
                        "source_entry_id": "0bb946ca-80e1-3970-9e3c-41c1f74f356b",
                        "source_sense_id": "8c83e5c0-1b42-3f8b-b645-eadf69e506f8",
                        "target_lang_word": "australopithecine",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "australopithecine",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "03b8b263-5350-33cc-8fca-ddcc87a6ac1d",
                                        "entry_id": "700f34b7-1b59-3442-8564-2713f51e5f5f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of several extinct hominids, belonging to the genera Australopithecus and Paranthropus in the subtribe Australopithecina when seen as distinct, and sometimes other closely related genera."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f4e0843a-827c-4dda-9f30-0abcf0ad8340",
                                                "sense_id": "03b8b263-5350-33cc-8fca-ddcc87a6ac1d",
                                                "text": "It is as if there were enshrined in these legends a racial memory of the Australopithicines who came close but never did make it to full humanity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1e7c1c6d-9458-4185-93b1-764bfe135ec6",
                                                "sense_id": "03b8b263-5350-33cc-8fca-ddcc87a6ac1d",
                                                "text": "Australopithecines came in several varieties, some slender and gracile, like Raymond Dart's Taung child, others more sturdy and robust, but all were capable of walking upright."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "59ac99b3-f615-4f57-ac2c-e259e23dd61c",
                                                "sense_id": "03b8b263-5350-33cc-8fca-ddcc87a6ac1d",
                                                "text": "Caspari and Lee carried out comparisons ranging from ancient hominins such as australopithecines through to Neanderthals and Cro-Magnons, assessing the ratios of young adults to old adults."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "australopithecine",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dc4e1bd9-8f4f-3e0e-8bd8-b110a0cd0419",
                                        "entry_id": "e18eaf36-6dea-3981-85b6-4b629ed58623",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or pertaining to these hominids."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e9efe30d-1df1-4653-94ca-5dc694295af2",
                        "source_entry_id": "0bb946ca-80e1-3970-9e3c-41c1f74f356b",
                        "source_sense_id": "8c83e5c0-1b42-3f8b-b645-eadf69e506f8",
